  "LPG production is in kb/d (EIA; 2014 is the last year of its series) and consumption and trade in Mt; the headline consumption carries kb/d in brackets (Atlas conversion: 11.60 barrels per tonne, the ratio of EIA's series for United States LPG consumption in thousand barrels per day and in thousand metric tons (the same in every year from 1980 to 2019); other countries differ slightly). Prices on the atlas are in USD per US gallon: at that ratio and 42 US gallons per barrel (EIA, units and calculators) one tonne of LPG is 487 US gallons, so a price per gallon times 487 is a price per tonne (Atlas conversion).",
  "Customs data record 0.00769 Mt of LPG exports from Iran in 2024, against 8.44 Mt in 2022 (CEPII BACI). Unrecorded shipments, or cargoes declared under other origins, are a plausible cause; it is not established here. The atlas has no free source that measures this gap, so it is not quantified.",
  "Customs data record 2.75 Mt of LPG from Oman to China in 2024 (86% of its recorded exports, CEPII BACI). The origin of these cargoes is not checked against an independent source: while Iran's exports are unrecorded, cargoes of other origins declared under Oman may account for part of this volume; it is not established here, and the atlas has no free source to measure it.",
  "Customs data record 6.98 Mt of LPG from the United Arab Emirates to China in 2024 (40% of its recorded exports, CEPII BACI). The origin of these cargoes is not checked against an independent source: while Iran's exports are unrecorded, cargoes of other origins declared under the United Arab Emirates may account for part of this volume; it is not established here, and the atlas has no free source to measure it."
